@startuml
title Consolidated Multi-Hybrid Cloud DFS Architecture with Operations Layers

actor User

package "Multi-Hybrid Cloud Environment" {

  cloud "Cloud Region 1" {
    rectangle "DFS Partition 1" as Part1
    rectangle "Observability\nDashboard & Metrics" as Obs1
    rectangle "Autoscaling Controller" as Auto1
    rectangle "Security Layer\n(Network Policies, RBAC)" as Sec1
  }

  cloud "Cloud Region 2" {
    rectangle "DFS Partition 2" as Part2
    rectangle "Observability\nDashboard & Metrics" as Obs2
    rectangle "Autoscaling Controller" as Auto2
    rectangle "Security Layer\n(Network Policies, RBAC)" as Sec2
  }

  package "On-Prem Data Center" {
    rectangle "DFS Partition 3" as Part3
    rectangle "Observability\nDashboard & Metrics" as Obs3
    rectangle "Autoscaling Controller" as Auto3
    rectangle "Security Layer\n(Network Policies, RBAC)" as Sec3
  }
}

User --> Part1 : File access
User --> Part2
User --> Part3

Part1 --> Obs1 : Emit logs & metrics
Part1 --> Auto1 : Send scaling metrics
Part1 --> Sec1 : Enforce security policies

Part2 --> Obs2 : Emit logs & metrics
Part2 --> Auto2 : Send scaling metrics
Part2 --> Sec2 : Enforce security policies

Part3 --> Obs3 : Emit logs & metrics
Part3 --> Auto3 : Send scaling metrics
Part3 --> Sec3 : Enforce security policies

Obs1 --> Obs2
Obs2 --> Obs3 : Centralized monitoring aggregation

Auto1 --> Part1 : Scale up/down instances
Auto2 --> Part2
Auto3 --> Part3

Sec1 -[#blue]-> Sec2 : Policy sync & audit logs
Sec2 -[#blue]-> Sec3

@enduml